    "status": "present",
    "value": "Two soups, A and B, each start with n millilitres. Repeatedly, one of four servings is chosen uniformly at random: 100 mL of A and 0 of B, 75 and 25, 50 and 50, or 25 and 75. If a serving asks for more than what remains, serve what is left. Stop as soon as either soup is empty. Return the probability that A runs out first plus half the probability that both run out at the same time."
  },
